<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n113796" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χερμ-άς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">άδος</span>,
			ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>large pebble</i> or <i>stone,</i> esp. for throwing or
			slinging, <i>sling-stone,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τηλεβόλος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>P.</u>
					3.49
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀκριόεσσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Th.</u>
					300
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κραταίβολος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ba.</u>
					1096
				</span></i>
			: of <i>pebbles</i> on the seabeach, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				2.695
			</span></i> (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στία</span>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				7.693
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Apollonid.
			</span></i>); also in later Prose, <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				9.21
			</span></i>, al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> in
			later Poets, <i>large block of stone,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Lyc.
				20
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				616
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				7.371
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Crin.
			</span></i>).</div>
